// The project-level default for Ferry's signing settings.
//
// These three lines make a fresh clone build with no Apple developer
// team. `scripts/gate.sh mac` and the README's build command both rely
// on this. The app is ad hoc signed: it runs, but macOS treats each
// rebuild as a new app, so the Keychain and the local network prompt ask
// again each time.
CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED = NO
CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY =
DEVELOPMENT_TEAM =

// An owner with an Apple team overrides the three lines above without
// editing this tracked file. Create macos/Local.xcconfig (gitignored)
// with:
//
//   CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED = YES
//   CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY = Apple Development
//   DEVELOPMENT_TEAM = <team ID>
//
// A setting later in this file wins, so Local.xcconfig, included last,
// overrides the defaults above. `#include?`, with the question mark,
// does nothing when the file is absent, so a fresh clone with no
// Local.xcconfig still builds. See CONTRIBUTING.md.
#include? "Local.xcconfig"
